    <string name="about_changelog_title">Changelog</string>
    <string name="about_changelog_v112_title">v1.1.2 · Dynamic Host Device &amp; System Probing</string>
    <string name="about_changelog_v112_desc">• Eliminated hardcoded host device strings; introduced dynamic DeviceInfoHelper\n• Auto-detects OEM marketing model names (vivo/iQOO, Xiaomi/Redmi, OPPO/OnePlus, Honor, etc.)\n• Dynamically probes Linux kernel device codenames and Android OS version at runtime\n• Interactive device info chip with click-to-copy full hardware specs &amp; CPU ABI to clipboard\n• Decoupled header subtitles and synchronized runtime host initialization logs</string>
    <string name="about_changelog_v111_title">v1.1.1 · AIDL IPC Service Integration</string>
    <string name="about_changelog_v111_desc">• Added IGh0stOverlayService AIDL inter-process communication interface\n• Exposed public Service (OVERLAY_SERVICE) for external modules/apps to interface with manager\n• Supports remote Root probing, partition status query, upperdir retrieval, mount &amp; unmount\n• Supports remote storage sync (syncStorage) and soft reboot (restartZygote)</string>
    <string name="about_changelog_v110_title">v1.1.0 · Brand-New About Page &amp; Navigation Redesign</string>
    <string name="about_changelog_v110_desc">• Replaced test payloads tab with a comprehensive, modern About page\n• Reordered bottom navigation: Control, Partitions, Logs, Settings, About\n• Prominently display vector app logo with build-time Git commit hash pill\n• Added anti-fraud / permanently free notice and one-click GitHub repo link\n• Added complete version changelog timeline with full localization</string>
    <string name="about_changelog_v103_title">v1.0.3 · Multi-SU Support &amp; Legacy Kernel Adaptation</string>
    <string name="about_changelog_v103_desc">• Added auto-detection for KernelSU, Magisk, APatch, and absolute su paths\n• Adapted step-based loop allocation for legacy kernels (Linux 4.14+), fixing loop attach conflicts\n• Auto-sync SELinux contexts on OverlayFS mount, resolving permission denied (error=13)\n• Guided image creation prompts before mounting, preventing implicit disk formatting</string>
    <string name="about_changelog_v102_title">v1.0.2 · Loop Teardown &amp; Idempotent Recovery</string>
    <string name="about_changelog_v102_desc">• Explicitly release associated loop devices upon unmount\n• Collision-free loop device scanning (30..99) preventing EBUSY\n• Removed aggressive auto-resize; lowered minimum image size to 16 MiB</string>
    <string name="about_changelog_v101_title">v1.0.1 · Pipelined Execution &amp; Debounce Protection</string>
    <string name="about_changelog_v101_desc">• Concurrent multi-partition pipelined mounting for significantly faster startup\n• Added UI debounce and thread-level state refresh guard\n• Integrated GitHub Actions CI/CD automated build pipelines</string>
    <string name="about_changelog_v100_title">v1.0.0 · Initial Open Source Release</string>
    <string name="about_changelog_v100_desc">• First official open-source release\n• Flash-free system partition takeover via OverlayFS\n• Skeuomorphic liquid glass navigation bar &amp; Material You theming</string>
